      [
        "Language grounding",
        "π0.5 appeared better than ACT and SmolVLA at colour-conditioned object selection and novel colour prompts.",
        "No trial counts or success percentages were reported for this comparison.",
        "Recorded here as a qualitative finding."
      ],
      [
        "Execution style",
        "π0.5 was more confident, SmolVLA was often jerky, and ACT tended to be hesitant.",
        "The comparison is descriptive rather than numerical.",
        "Also summarized on the Few-Shot sheet."
      ],
      [
        "Grasping consistency",
        "Approaching from above, from the side, or pushing the object before grasping likely introduced strategy inconsistency.",
        "No numerical effect size was reported.",
        "Recorded here as dataset-design context."
      ],
      [
        "Recovery starts",
        "Both 100-episode consistency datasets used 20% non-home or recovery starts.",
